From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] api: no trust by the peer address for requests sent by pages
 of other sites

is_authenticated() lets in every request from a loopback, private,
link-local or Tailscale peer address without a session. The address is
the one of the client, not of the page that made the request: a page of
another site opened in a browser of a LAN client could call the panel
API, including POST /ubus with file.exec of any command (the answer to
the CORS preflight allows any origin, and the response could be read). A
name of that site that resolves to the router address after the page has
loaded (DNS rebinding) passed the same way.

A request is now not trusted by the peer address when the browser marks
it as sent by another site (Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site), when its Origin
is null or names another host and port than Host, or when Host is a
domain name outside the local names (an IP literal, localhost, a single
label, .lan, .local, .home.arpa, .internal, .ts.net). Such a request
needs a session or the agent token, as one from a public address.
Requests without these headers (the CLI forwarded over 127.0.0.1, curl,
scripts) and the panel opened by an address or a local name are not
affected.

New test: test_foreign_browser_request.

